# The fast gates, on everything. No lint-staged: these four total about
# five seconds on this repo, which is less than the machinery to run
# them on only the staged files would cost to maintain. Revisit if the
# suite grows.
#
# format:check rather than `pnpm format`, and the reason is specific to
# there being no lint-staged here: a bare `pnpm format` in a hook
# rewrites the whole tree and leaves those changes unstaged, so the
# commit ships the unformatted version anyway. Failing and asking you to
# run `pnpm format` is honest.
#
# This is NOT an argument against `prettier --write` inside lint-staged -
# lint-staged has added its tasks' modifications to the commit by itself
# since v10, and warns if you add a manual `git add`. If lint-staged ever
# earns its place here, --write is the right call there.
pnpm typecheck
pnpm lint
pnpm format:check
pnpm test
